-# crud_notes
+# Notes API
+
+This project implements the confirmed starter behavior: create and list
+in-memory notes.  There are intentionally no delete routes or functions, and
+it has no Redis dependency.
+
+## Run
+
+Requires Python 3.11 or later. No third-party packages are needed.
+
+```bash
+python -m app
+```
+
+The server listens on `http://127.0.0.1:8000`.
+
+```bash
+curl -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/notes \\
+  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\
+  -d '{"text":"Study chapter 1"}'
+curl http://127.0.0.1:8000/notes
+```
+
+`POST /notes` accepts `{"text": "..."}` and returns `201`; `GET /notes`
+returns all notes. Text is trimmed and must contain 1 to 10,000 characters.
+
+## Test
+
+```bash
+python -m unittest discover -s tests -p 'test_*.py' -v
+```
+
+The repository's original pytest-style smoke test is retained. The unittest
+suite covers the same confirmed create/list behavior and validation without
+requiring external dependencies.
+
+## Acceptance evidence
+
+- Tests pass: `python -m unittest discover -s tests -p 'test_*.py' -v`.
+- Application runs: `python -m app`, then use the `curl` commands above.
